thaumictinkerer.research.projecting_infusion.title=Infusion Enchantment: Projecting
thaumictinkerer.research.projecting_infusion.title.subtitle=Spears are better than swords
thaumictinkerer.research.projecting_infusion.stage.1=[WIP]
thaumictinkerer.research.projecting_infusion.stage.2=[WIP]

# -- EQUIPMENT: Infusion Enchantment: Wrath
thaumictinkerer.research.wrath_infusion.title=Infusion Enchantment: Wrath
thaumictinkerer.research.wrath_infusion.title.subtitle=When your weapon is still not cutting it
thaumictinkerer.research.wrath_infusion.stage.1=I've always thought to myself... "How about something that just simply adds more damage?". It's now finally time for me to make that happen.
thaumictinkerer.research.wrath_infusion.stage.2=The Wrath infusion enchantment, simply put, makes my weapon deal more damage and is compatible with regular enchantments that affect damage.<BR>Like other infusion enchantments, it can be applied multiple times to the same item, but each rank has an increased essentia cost when crafted.<PAGE>§oWrath§r<DIV>The infusion will first apply a base damage of +0.5 to the tool, and then add an additional +0.5 damage per rank (Wrath I would give +1 damage).<DIV>§oRanks§r: 1-5<BR>§oTarget§r: weapon

# -- EQUIPMENT: Sigil of Consuming
thaumictinkerer.research.consuming_sigil.title=Sigil of Consuming
thaumictinkerer.research.consuming_sigil.title.subtitle=Don't ask questions, just consume
thaumictinkerer.research.consuming_sigil.stage.1=Long days of mining often yield few useful resources, but a significant amount of common materials.<BR>While a cactus or lava might be solutions, they are hardly portable.
thaumictinkerer.research.consuming_sigil.stage.2=I have devised a device that, when enabled, instantly destroys any common materials I might pick up.<BR>I can toggle this function by sneaking and interacting with the sigil.

# -- EQUIPMENT: Ring of Goliath's Might
thaumictinkerer.research.goliath_ring.title=Ring of Goliath's Might
thaumictinkerer.research.goliath_ring.title.subtitle=Weak to stone
thaumictinkerer.research.goliath_ring.stage.1=[WIP]
thaumictinkerer.research.goliath_ring.stage.2=[WIP]

# -- EQUIPMENT: Sword of the Condor
thaumictinkerer.research.condor_sword.title=Sword of the Condor
thaumictinkerer.research.condor_sword.title.subtitle=The condor does not fear the storm
thaumictinkerer.research.condor_sword.stage.1=The Sword of the Zephyr has its uses, but its ability can be underwhelming compared to the other elemental tools. I should figure out how to improve it further.
thaumictinkerer.research.condor_sword.stage.2=I have successfully upgraded my Sword of the Zephyr into what I call the Sword of the Condor!<BR>This removes its old whirlwind ability and instead allows me to charge into the air. I can right-click to charge into the direction I'm looking at, I can do this in reverse while sneaking. When I do this several times, it will also allow me to fly around.

# -- EQUIPMENT: Talisman of Experience
thaumictinkerer.research.xp_talisman.title=Talisman of Experience
thaumictinkerer.research.xp_talisman.title.subtitle=Death cannot undo me
thaumictinkerer.research.xp_talisman.stage.1=[WIP]
thaumictinkerer.research.xp_talisman.stage.2=[WIP]

# -- MISC: Aquatic Alchemy
thaumictinkerer.research.aquatic_alchemy.title=Aquatic Alchemy
thaumictinkerer.research.aquatic_alchemy.title.subtitle=Ocean's bounty
thaumictinkerer.research.aquatic_alchemy.stage.1=The ocean has a plethora of materials that can only be found when venturing into its deepest depths.<BR>Alchemy should provide a means to create these materials from common components.
thaumictinkerer.research.aquatic_alchemy.stage.2=Using mundane ingredients, I can now artificially create my own prismarine shards, sea lanterns and sponges.

