thaumictinkerer.research.escape_sigil.stage.2=[WIP]

# -- MISC: Essentia Funnel
thaumictinkerer.research.essentia_funnel.title=Essentia Funnel
thaumictinkerer.research.essentia_funnel.title.subtitle=Topping the tank
thaumictinkerer.research.essentia_funnel.stage.1=The process of emptying essentia from jars is a truly frustrating experience. I either have to dump massive amounts of flux into the environment or rely on piping that can only be described as "somewhat functional".<BR>There must be a better way...
thaumictinkerer.research.essentia_funnel.stage.2=I have developed rudimentary funnel capable of rapidly transferring essentia from one jar to another.<BR>The essentia funnel must be placed directly on top of a hopper, with the hopper facing into the essentia container.<BR>I can then place a jar into the funnel, which will rapidly drain the contents of the jar.

# -- MISC: Everfull Bucket
thaumictinkerer.research.everfull_bucket.title=Everfull Bucket
thaumictinkerer.research.everfull_bucket.title.subtitle=A whole ocean could fit in it!
thaumictinkerer.research.everfull_bucket.stage.1=While the everful urn is useful around my base, the static nature of the device makes it difficult to utilize in more remote areas.
thaumictinkerer.research.everfull_bucket.stage.2=I have created a bucket that mimics the behavior of the everful urn, endlessly dispensing water at the cost vis pulled from the aura.<BR>The process is not quite as efficient as the urn. I estimate it consumes roughly twice the vis per bucket of water produced.

# -- MISC: Obsidia Terra
thaumictinkerer.research.terra_obsidian.title=Obsidia Terra
thaumictinkerer.research.terra_obsidian.title.subtitle=Green Obsidian
thaumictinkerer.research.terra_obsidian.stage.1=My attempts to contain certain powerful threats have been only moderately successful.<BR>Perhaps there is a way to further reinforce the already resilient nature of obsidian?
thaumictinkerer.research.terra_obsidian.stage.2=Who would have thought it was as simple as infusing terra crystals into obsidian?<BR>Obsidia Terra, as I have dubbed this material, is 2.5 times more resistant to explosions than normal obsidian, yet is significantly easier to harvest with a pickaxe. Certainly a material this robust could be used to contain powerful fel creatures.

# -- MISC: Thaumic Cake
thaumictinkerer.research.thaumic_cake.title=Thaumic Cake
thaumictinkerer.research.thaumic_cake.title.subtitle=Let them eat cake!
thaumictinkerer.research.thaumic_cake.stage.1=People constantly tell me that I cannot have my cake and eat it too, but what do they know?<BR>As the very world bends to my will, what better way to expend my precious time on this planet than to find a solution to this sever lack of cake.<BR>They might think me mad, but at least I'm not desperate enough to eat pie.
thaumictinkerer.research.thaumic_cake.stage.2=What's better than cake? More cake! What's better than more cake? Infinite cake!<BR>My colleagues think I am mad for eating infinitely regrowing cake, but what do they know? It tastes fine to me!

# -- MISC: Thaumic Restorer
thaumictinkerer.research.thaumic_restorer.title=Thaumic Restorer
thaumictinkerer.research.thaumic_restorer.title.subtitle=Undoing the damage you've done
thaumictinkerer.research.thaumic_restorer.stage.1=If physical objects can be broken down into essentia, then could essentia be use to reconstruct damaged items?<BR>If so, this could significantly reduce the cost of upkeep for my tools and armor.
thaumictinkerer.research.thaumic_restorer.stage.2=[WIP]

# -- MISC: Timetwister Stopwatch
thaumictinkerer.research.recall_stopwatch.title=Timetwister Stopwatch
thaumictinkerer.research.recall_stopwatch.title.subtitle=Back to the Past
thaumictinkerer.research.recall_stopwatch.stage.1=With the success of the sigil of escape, I cannot help but wonder what else could be possible...
thaumictinkerer.research.recall_stopwatch.stage.2=I have designed a device capable of rending the very fabric of reality and restoring matter to its previous state.<BR>Upon activation, a timer for 60 seconds starts.<BR>During this time I can move and act freely. Once the 60 seconds has expired, I will be recalled back to the location I activated the stopwatch, restoring my health and hunger to their previous values.
thaumictinkerer.research.recall_stopwatch.addenda.1=It appears that the stopwatch only seems to effect my physical body. Any items damaged or destroyed during the timer will not be restored to their previous states.

# -- MISC: Umbral Rose Bush
thaumictinkerer.research.umbral_rosebush.title=Umbral Rose Bush
thaumictinkerer.research.umbral_rosebush.title.subtitle=Save the squids!
thaumictinkerer.research.umbral_rosebush.stage.1=There's no sight more pathetic than a soggy Thaumaturge. Constantly having to venture into the oceans to find and defeat squid for ink sacs is becoming an incredible annoyance.<BR>Thaumaturgy has yet to fail me, so there must be an answer I can devise.
thaumictinkerer.research.umbral_rosebush.stage.2=I have created a flower that grows roses that can be crushed into black dye.<BR>Though the plant grows slowly, using shears I can harvest individual roses, giving me a nearly infinite supply of ink without the need to get wet.

# -- NECROMANCY
thaumictinkerer.research.necromancy.title=Necromancy
thaumictinkerer.research.necromancy.title.subtitle=Necronomicon not included
thaumictinkerer.research.necromancy.stage.1=On my travels I have encountered strange caged devices in underground dungeons that appear to create creatures from nothing.<BR>Because all creatures are composed of essentia, I cannot help but I wonder if I could create a device that can replicate this process using essentia.
thaumictinkerer.research.necromancy.stage.2=Though the process is closer to reconstruction than necromancy, empty vessels created through this process rapidly decay unless bound with an artificial soul.<BR>Using the Tablet of Necromancy and a properly constructed altar, I can use essentia to construct an empty vessel and bind an artificial soul to the created flesh.<BR>With the altar properly constructed, I merely need to place an entity soul into tablet and place the correct catalysts onto the surrounding pedestals.<BR>Once all the components are in place, the altar will begin drawing essentia from nearby sources automatically.<BR>Once enough essentia has been consumed, the creature will spawn directly above the tablet, slightly reducing the strength of the entity soul.
thaumictinkerer.research.necromancy.addenda.1=It appears that the process of creating creatures is fully autonimous, as though the entity soul wants to be bound to a vessel.<BR>Should I wish to disable the altar or stop the spawning process I can apply a redstone signal to the tablet.

# -- NECROMANCY: ALIEN SOUL
thaumictinkerer.research.alien_soul.title=Soul: Alien
thaumictinkerer.research.alien_soul.title.subtitle=Void Spirits
thaumictinkerer.research.alien_soul.stage.1=My attempts to raise extra-dimensional creatures have largely been fruitless.<BR>There is just something different about how their spirits embody living flesh.
thaumictinkerer.research.alien_soul.stage.2=With this new soul I can now bind the souls of otherworldly beings to constructed vessels.<BR>However, the soul has proven to be much more fragile than expected, fading roughly twice as fast as the peaceful or hostile entity souls.

# -- NECROMANCY: ARCANE SOUL
thaumictinkerer.research.arcane_soul.title=Soul: Arcane
thaumictinkerer.research.arcane_soul.title.subtitle=Magical Spirits
thaumictinkerer.research.arcane_soul.stage.1=My testing has shown that the sentient creatures are significantly more difficult to summon than those without significant cognitive processes.<BR>Where there is a will, there is another roadblock to overcome in my research...
thaumictinkerer.research.arcane_soul.stage.2=With this new soul type, I can bind the souls of sentient creatures to empty vessels.<BR>However, the soul has proven to be much more fragile than expected, fading roughly twice as fast as the peaceful or hostile entity souls.

# -- NECROMANCY: DEMONIC SOUL
thaumictinkerer.research.demonic_soul.title=Soul: Demonic
thaumictinkerer.research.demonic_soul.title.subtitle=Pyre Spirits
thaumictinkerer.research.demonic_soul.stage.1=I suppose it should have been obvious in retrospect. Creatures of the nether do not have souls like those found in the overworld.<BR>However, if the nether truly is some type of afterlife for this world, then those creatures must have some similarity to what I have found thus far.
thaumictinkerer.research.demonic_soul.stage.2=With this new soul type I can now bind the souls of creatures from the nether to empty vessels.<BR>However, the soul has proven to be much more fragile than expected, fading roughly twice as fast as the peaceful or hostile entity souls.

# -- NECROMANCY: ELDRITCH SOUL
thaumictinkerer.research.eldritch_soul.title=Soul: Eldritch
thaumictinkerer.research.eldritch_soul.title.subtitle=Reticent Spirits
thaumictinkerer.research.eldritch_soul.stage.1=Some creatures are completely beyond what the entity souls I have created thus far can handle.<BR>As the strength of a creature increases, the fragility of the soul also increases...
thaumictinkerer.research.eldritch_soul.stage.2=I barely managed to stabilize this new soul type long enough for it to become tangible.<BR>Judging by the fragility of the eldritch soul, it may only have one use before fully dissipating. I can only imagine the creatures I can create with this...

# -- NECROMANCY: HOSTILE SOUL
thaumictinkerer.research.hostile_soul.title=Soul: Hostile
thaumictinkerer.research.hostile_soul.title.subtitle=Maddening Spirits
thaumictinkerer.research.hostile_soul.stage.1=Thus far, I have only managed to reconstruct relatively weak creatures, generally those who have little to no will of their own beyond basic animal instincts.<BR>To go further I will need a new type of soul...
thaumictinkerer.research.hostile_soul.stage.2=I have managed to create a new entity soul capable of binding hostile creatures commonly encountered in the overworld.

# -- NECROMANCY: TAINTED SOUL
thaumictinkerer.research.tainted_soul.title=Soul: Tainted
thaumictinkerer.research.tainted_soul.title.subtitle=Parasitical Spirits
thaumictinkerer.research.tainted_soul.stage.1=Tainted beings are so unlike any other creatures I have encountered.<BR>The way taint and flux can infect and infest other creatures, leads me to believe that there is a connection I have not yet discovered.
thaumictinkerer.research.tainted_soul.stage.2=I have managed to create a new entity soul capable of binding tainted creates to empty vessels.<BR>I should take care with these creatures as many of them can cause irreversible damage if left unchecked.

# GroovyScript
